   "displayId": "textTurn_exploreDataFromNL_1794707200000_closing",
   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Governments spend very different amounts on heritage: about $21 a person in the typical country of the 72 that report.** The highest:\n\n- **Belgium:** $369 a person (2023)\n- **Malta:** $350 a person (2023)\n- **Bolivia:** $297 a person (2023)\n- **Finland:** $265 a person (2023)\n- **Croatia:** $245 a person (2023)\n\nAt the other end, 13 countries spend under $1 a person. Figures are public spending on cultural and natural heritage in constant 2017 purchasing-power dollars, each country's latest from 2020–2024. Source: UIS, February 2026 release; indicator HEXPCSTPPPCAP.HER.PU.",
